      "content": "but aren't those McKinsey studies pretty criticized for just showing correlation rather than causation? like, maybe successful companies just have more resources to spend on DEI, not the other way around. i've seen some articles saying that when you control for other factors, the actual 'diversity dividend' mostly disappears. what's the deal with the counter-evidence to that?",
